      <description><![CDATA[<!DOCTYPE html><html><head><meta charset="utf-8"><style>html{color-scheme:light dark}body{font:13px/1.5 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'SF Pro Text',system-ui,sans-serif;color:#18181b;background:transparent;margin:0;padding:4px 2px}ul{margin:0 0 10px;padding-left:18px}li{margin:0 0 6px}p{margin:0 0 10px}h4{font-size:12px;font-weight:600;color:#52525b;margin:16px 0 6px;padding-top:10px;border-top:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,.08)}code{font:12px ui-monospace,'SF Mono',monospace;background:rgba(0,0,0,.06);padding:1px 4px;border-radius:6px}@media (prefers-color-scheme:dark){body{color:#f4f4f5}h4{color:#a1a1aa;border-top-color:rgba(255,255,255,.12)}code{background:rgba(255,255,255,.1)}}</style></head><body><ul><li>Full screen: the window controls stay in while you move down from the menu bar to click them; they follow where the row really is instead of a fixed guess.</li></ul><h4>Also in 2.23.33</h4><ul><li>A new version waits quietly in the sidebar footer: one muted line with Install and Later instead of a big yellow button. Later puts it away (a small dot on the refresh icon remembers it) until you click there or a newer version arrives.</li></ul><h4>Also in 2.23.32</h4><ul><li>A chat whose turn has ended but whose ducklings or background shells are still running keeps its working look in the sidebar, its tab, Home and the palette, so a busy stream never looks finished.</li></ul></body></html>]]></description>
